It is the next morning.
I am at the large registration office today.
There are many people in here.
I have my passport and my papers in my bag.
Everything is ready for my registration.
I stand by a red machine.
I press a button.
The machine gives me a small number slip.
What is my number?
I look at the paper.
I have number fifty-nine.
It is a rather high number.
A large screen on the wall shows a number.
The screen only shows number twenty-one.
I have plenty of time.
I find an empty chair.
I sit down with my papers.
Now I wait for my turn.
